    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 14 tests pass, including both `Cp07Tests` (the registration-date checkpoint), and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied, the server sets it to its current date, and it is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, this field appears on both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`), generated as a `java.time.LocalDate` (same as the existing `birthDate`), which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name automatically in both directions.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Added a `defaultRegistrationDate(...)` step that sets `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when the client omitted it; a supplied value is preserved. `updateOwner` intentionally leaves the existing value untouched.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so this column is what makes persistence work; the other variants are updated for consistency.\n\nThe two behaviors verified by `Cp07Tests`: `coreDefaultsTotoday` (defaults to today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (keeps `2020-06-15`) both pass, and the rest of the suite remains green.",
